From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim Gardner <tim.gardner@canonical.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Nov 2012 12:09:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] UBUNTU: SAUCE: (no-up) Revert "VFS: don't do protected
 {sym,hard}links by default"

This reverts commit 561ec64ae67ef25cac8d72bb9c4bfc955edfd415.

BugLink: http://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/1084192

Reverting this in the kernel as opposed to adding a sysctl
to the procps package guarentees that this regression will be
propagated to the Raring LTS kernel.

Signed-off-by: Tim Gardner <tim.gardner@canonical.com>
Ledger-Change: C-00010
Ledger-Origin: ubuntu@ecdd4841bbaff59eec05ca8cd8707d62b1f05ff0
---
 fs/namei.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/fs/namei.c b/fs/namei.c
index e45e30603215..a943ee5ccb5d 100644
--- a/fs/namei.c
+++ b/fs/namei.c
@@ -1201,8 +1201,8 @@ static inline void put_link(struct nameidata *nd)
 		path_put(&last->link);
 }
 
-static int sysctl_protected_symlinks __read_mostly;
-static int sysctl_protected_hardlinks __read_mostly;
+static int sysctl_protected_symlinks __read_mostly = 1;
+static int sysctl_protected_hardlinks __read_mostly = 1;
 static int sysctl_protected_fifos __read_mostly;
 static int sysctl_protected_regular __read_mostly;
 
